ready1_open_rewrite.raw_answer_text:
\textbf{Solution:}

\[
\begin{aligned}
&\because a=-1, b=-2 \\
&\therefore y=x^2-2x+3 \\
&\text{when} x=0, y=3 \\
&\therefore A(0, 3) \\
&\text{Let the line} AB: y=kx+b' \\
&\because B(-3, 0) \\
&\therefore
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
b'=3 \\
-3k+b'=0
\end{array}
\right. \\
&\therefore
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
k=1 \\
b'=3
\end{array}
\right. \\
&\therefore \text{The equation of line} AB \text{is} y=x+3 \\
&\because DP \parallel \text{the y-axis}, \\
&\therefore P, O \text{have the same x-coordinate} t \\
&\therefore p(t, -t^2-2t+3), O(t, t+3) \\
&\therefore d=-t^2-2t+3-(t+3) \\
&=-t^2-3t \\
&\therefore d=\boxed{-t^2-3t}
\end{aligned}
\]

